  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the cube in the first octant with sides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;and OR of length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>, along the x-axis, y-axis and z-axis, respectively, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> is the origin. Let <math><mi>S</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> be the centre of the cube and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;be the vertex of the cube opposite to the origin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;lies on the diagonal&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>T</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is ______.",
